 "title": "is 'the tight end never narrows' a property of these windows or of how a band is built?",
 "verdict": "tight_end_dead_by_construction_family_should_stop_publishing_tight_pass_checks",
 "verdict_reason": "lo is the MINIMUM of a nested prefix (BAND_PCT 0..100) and the endpoint's draw exponent is positive on every published family (gamma 0.348..0.647), so the lower endpoint only moves outward and m = |lo|(top)/|lo|(base) cannot go below 1 unless every draw were positive -- which never happens on this population (140 published lower ends, all >= 1.0, 39 exactly 1.0).  The exact ones are the degenerate branch, not a window that narrowed and stopped: one seed away they lift to 1.11..1.20.  A tight-pass check on this family can therefore only ever return zero"
}
